6. Consistency in Riak KV

Riak uses replication and quorum parameters to balance consistency and availability.

Example request:

curl -X PUT \
'http://localhost:8098/buckets/students/keys/101?w=2'

w=2 means the write should receive acknowledgements from two replicas.

Read:

curl \
'http://localhost:8098/buckets/students/keys/101?r=2'

r=2 requests responses from two replicas.

Common concepts:

N → Number of replicas
W → Required write acknowledgements
R → Required read acknowledgements

Higher R/W values can improve consistency but may increase latency and reduce availability during failures.

