Part B – Neo4j
11. Student-Course-Department Graph

Open Neo4j and create nodes:

CREATE (s:Student {id:101,name:'Rahul'}),
       (c:Course {id:'BCA',name:'BCA'}),
       (d:Department {id:'D1',name:'Computer Science'});
Relationships
MATCH (s:Student {id:101}),
      (c:Course {id:'BCA'}),
      (d:Department {id:'D1'})
CREATE (s)-[:ENROLLED_IN]->(c),
       (c)-[:BELONGS_TO]->(d);
View graph
MATCH (n)-[r]->(m)
RETURN n,r,m;

Neo4j Browser displays the graph visually.

